Write a function to calculate the average of all elements in a list of lists of integers.

The function is named `average_of_list_of_lists/1` and takes a single argument: a list of lists of integers. It should return the arithmetic mean of all integers across all sublists, as a float.

- The input will always contain at least one sublist with at least one element, so division by zero is not a concern.
